      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a really interesting proposal, so I’d like to give it a little up!\n\nIt would make it possible to improve the immersion aspect and make the overall experience feel much more visually cohesive. On my end, I’ve developed my own visual interaction system, and unfortunately, the blue highlight clashes with it, which affects the overall look.\n\nPersonally, I also feel that the blue highlight can sometimes break immersion and doesn’t necessarily fit very well with certain immersive environments.\n\nHaving the ability to disable or customize it would be really great.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-04-23T14:15:19.467Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, when a user enters the interaction range an interactive game object in a world, VRChat displays a blue halo around it.\n\nUdon can control this highlight with `InputManager.EnableObjectHighlight`, though it's unreliable and undocumented. It turns the highlight on and off, but the game object loses or regains its highlight if the user enters the interaction range. Worlds can work around this by calling `EnableObjectHighlight` every Update.\n\nUdon should be able to control an object's highlight state to a greater extent.",
